{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '115,285p'\"","aggregated_output":"   115\t;; =============================================================================\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn make-indexer\n   118\t  \"The indexer for one session: `observer`, attached to `program-out`\n   119\t   beside the evaluator's; a complete-retention local log with its\n   120\t   transactor (dao.space.transactor requires memory-log retention); an\n   121\t   intake with a `dao.jing` pool observer over it; and `content-store`, the\n   122\t   `dao.jing` byte store publications materialize into.  `session-token` is\n   123\t   the shell's stable token, recorded as provenance; `publish-opts` reach\n   124\t   `transactor/publish!` as-is.\n   125\t\n   126\t   The intake is complete-retention too: `publish-index!` appends every\n   127\t   node blob before the manifest and the round drains only after it\n   128\t   returns, so an evicting intake would lose the head of any publication\n   129\t   larger than its capacity and that publication could never complete.\"\n   130\t  [{:keys [observer session-token content-store publish-opts]}]\n   131\t  (let [log #(:dao.stream/handle\n   132\t               (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type\n   133\t                                    memory-log/transport-type}))\n   134\t        local (log)\n   135\t        intake (log)]\n   136\t    {:observer observer\n   137\t     :transactor (transactor/create! {:local-stream local\n   138\t                                      :intake-pool [intake]\n   139\t                                      :name \"yin.repl.index\"})\n   140\t     :pool (jing/observer-state\n   141\t             [{:stream intake\n   142\t               :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   143\t                         (stream/cursor intake :dao.stream/oldest))}])\n   144\t     :content-store content-store\n   145\t     :session-token session-token\n   146\t     :publish-opts publish-opts\n   147\t     :next-e datom/first-user-id\n   148\t     :transactions 0\n   149\t     :published 0\n   150\t     :manifest-address nil\n   151\t     :lost? false\n   152\t     :failure nil}))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn- commit\n   156\t  \"Commit one packet as one transaction.  A packet that could not be\n   157\t   projected or committed is consumed and recorded as the failure, never\n   158\t   counted.\"\n   159\t  [ix packet round]\n   160\t  (try\n   161\t    (let [{:keys [tx-data next-e root]}\n   162\t          (packet->tx-data packet\n   163\t                           (:next-e ix)\n   164\t                           {:session-token (:session-token ix), :round round})\n   165\t          answer (transactor/transact! (:transactor ix) tx-data)]\n   166\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   167\t        [(-> ix\n   168\t             (assoc :next-e next-e)\n   169\t             (update :transactions inc))\n   170\t         true]\n   171\t        [(assoc ix\n   172\t                :failure {:round round\n   173\t                          :root root\n   174\t                          :stage :transact\n   175\t                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n   176\t         false]))\n   177\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   178\t      [(assoc ix\n   179\t              :failure {:round round\n   180\t                        :stage :project\n   181\t                        :message (ex-message e)})\n   182\t       false])))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- materialize\n   186\t  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers the pool state\n   187\t   and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what it met.\"\n   188\t  [content-store pool]\n   189\t  (loop [pool pool]\n   190\t    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n   191\t      (case signal\n   192\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:state r))\n   193\t        :dao.stream/blocked [(:state r) nil]\n   194\t        [(cond-> (:state r)\n   195\t           (= :dao.stream/gap signal)\n   196\t           (jing/adopt-cursor (:member r) (:cursor r)))\n   197\t         signal]))))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn- publish\n   201\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction, drain\n   202\t   them into the store, and read the manifest back from it.  Only a\n   203\t   publication whose manifest the store answers becomes the reported one,\n   204\t   covering `:published` transactions.\"\n   205\t  [ix round]\n   206\t  (try\n   207\t    (let [{:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! (:transactor ix)\n   208\t                                                          (:publish-opts ix))\n   209\t          [pool defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) (:pool ix))\n   210\t          ix (assoc ix :pool pool)]\n   211\t      (if defect\n   212\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   213\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   214\t            (assoc ix\n   215\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   216\t                   :published (:transactions ix)))))\n   217\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   218\t      (assoc ix\n   219\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(defn- consume\n   223\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   224\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   225\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   226\t  [indexer f]\n   227\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   228\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   229\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   230\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   231\t      (case status\n   232\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   233\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   234\t        ix))))\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t(defn step\n   238\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   239\t   for this observer, commit each, and publish when any was committed.  A\n   240\t   gap is recovered across, counted on the observer's `:ingress-gaps`, and\n   241\t   marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and every later one are never\n   242\t   called indexed.\"\n   243\t  [indexer round]\n   244\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   245\t                    (fn [ix packet] (first (commit ix packet round))))]\n   246\t    (if (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   247\t      (publish ix round)\n   248\t      ix)))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn skip\n   252\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   253\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran executes nothing,\n   254\t   so nothing is indexed.  A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   255\t  [indexer]\n   256\t  (consume indexer (fn [ix _packet] ix)))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn status\n   260\t  \"The indexer's state as the shell reports it.  It depends on the programs\n   261\t   evaluated, never on which evaluator ran them or on the shell's token,\n   262\t   so every VM reports the same status for the same inputs.\"\n   263\t  [indexer]\n   264\t  {:transactions (:transactions indexer)\n   265\t   :published? (and (some? (:manifest-address indexer))\n   266\t                    (= (:published indexer) (:transactions indexer)))\n   267\t   :lost? (:lost? indexer)\n   268\t   :gaps (:ingress-gaps (:observer indexer) 0)\n   269\t   :failure (:failure indexer)})\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t(defn notice\n   273\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   274\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   275\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   276\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   277\t   `:publish`.\"\n   278\t  [before after]\n   279\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   280\t    (cond\n   281\t      (:lost? after)\n   282\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   283\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   284\t\n   285\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
