{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '272,310p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc | sed -n '1,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"   272\t(defn notice\n   273\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   274\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   275\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   276\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   277\t   `:publish`.\"\n   278\t  [before after]\n   279\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   280\t    (cond\n   281\t      (:lost? after)\n   282\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   283\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   284\t\n   285\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n   286\t      (str \"Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (\"\n   287\t           (name stage) \" failed\"\n   288\t           (when-let [detail (or message (some-> outcome name))]\n   289\t             (str \": \" detail))\n   290\t           \")\"))))\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.memory-log\n     2\t  \"In-memory, unbounded, append-only DaoStream v2 transport: the\n     3\t   complete-retention local log.  Process-lifetime, not durable across\n     4\t   restart — a restarted process sees a new, empty logical stream with a\n     5\t   new identity.  Durability is dao.jing's job, not this transport's.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Retention is complete, and the absence of eviction is structural:\n     8\t   state is one vector dense from position 0, and this namespace contains\n     9\t   no expression that removes an element.  `gap` is therefore excluded\n    10\t   (`:oldest` is position 0 for the life of the stream), as are `full`\n    11\t   (no capacity is declared; the transport is logically unbounded and\n    12\t   refuses nothing) and `transport-error` (each operation is one\n    13\t   in-memory state transition that either completes and returns or does\n    14\t   not return — the contract's line between observable exhaustion and\n    15\t   fatal host failure, which lies outside the outcome algebra).\n    16\t\n    17\t   There are no attachments: every handle is the logical stream's owner,\n    18\t   so `cursor` never answers `:dao.stream/closed` and keeps minting after\n    19\t   close, and `attach!` is absent rather than excluded.  Values are held\n    20\t   by reference and never encoded, so no value is uncarriable.\n    21\t\n    22\t   Creation specification: `{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log}`.\n    23\t   The transport owns the `dao.stream.memory-log` namespace and declares\n    24\t   nothing in it, so any `:dao.stream.memory-log/…` key is rejected with\n    25\t   `:dao.stream/invalid-spec` — most importantly a capacity, which is the\n    26\t   knob this transport exists to make impossible.  Any other qualified\n    27\t   key is ignored per the open-map rule.\"\n    28\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(def transport-type :dao.stream/memory-log)\n    32\t\n    33\t(def ^:private own-namespace \"dao.stream.memory-log\")\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- result\n    37\t  [outcome]\n    38\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn- permitted-key?\n    42\t  \"The contract: `:dao.stream/type` is the dispatch key, and every other\n    43\t   key is qualified (dao.stream.md, *Creation*).  So an unqualified or\n    44\t   non-keyword key is a malformed specification rather than a foreign\n    45\t   extension the open-map rule would have us ignore.  A key in this\n    46\t   transport's own namespace names a knob that does not exist, since that\n    47\t   namespace is owned and empty.\"\n    48\t  [k]\n    49\t  (and (keyword? k)\n    50\t       (or (= :dao.stream/type k)\n    51\t           (and (some? (namespace k))\n    52\t                (not= own-namespace (namespace k))))))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn- valid-spec?\n    56\t  \"A map, typed as this transport, whose every key is permitted.  Foreign\n    57\t   qualified keys are ignored per the open-map rule; unqualified,\n    58\t   non-keyword, and own-namespace keys are rejected.\"\n    59\t  [spec]\n    60\t  (and (map? spec)\n    61\t       (= transport-type (:dao.stream/type spec))\n    62\t       (every? permitted-key? (keys spec))))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(defn- fresh-state\n    66\t  []\n    67\t  ;; As in the ring buffer, the logical identity is plain data — it\n    68\t  ;; travels in descriptors and cursors — never a host UUID object.\n    69\t  ;; A vector, dense from 0: positions are never reused and never\n    70\t  ;; dropped, and the tail is (count values).\n    71\t  (atom {:identity (str (random-uuid))\n    72\t         :values []\n    73\t         :closed? false}))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(deftype MemoryLogHandle\n    77\t  [state]\n    78\t\n    79\t  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n    80\t\n    81\t  (descriptor\n    82\t    [_]\n    83\t    (let [s @state]\n    84\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    85\t       :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type transport-type\n    86\t                               :dao.stream/identity (:identity s)}\n    87\t       :dao.stream/identity (:identity s)}))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    91\t\n    92\t  (cursor\n    93\t    [_ anchor]\n    94\t    (let [s @state]\n    95\t      ;; Every handle is the logical stream's owner: there is no\n    96\t      ;; attachment to be closed, and an owner keeps minting cursors\n    97\t      ;; after close so retained history stays readable.\n    98\t      (case anchor\n    99\t        ;; Complete retention: :oldest is the origin, before the first\n   100\t        ;; append and after close alike.\n   101\t        :dao.stream/oldest\n   102\t        (assoc (result :dao.stream/ok)\n   103\t               :dao.stream/cursor\n   104\t               {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity (:identity s)\n   105\t                :dao.stream.memory-log/position 0})\n   106\t        :dao.stream/newest\n   107\t        (assoc (result :dao.stream/ok)\n   108\t               :dao.stream/cursor\n   109\t               {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity (:identity s)\n   110\t                :dao.stream.memory-log/position (count (:values s))})\n   111\t        (result :dao.stream/invalid-anchor))))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t  (next\n   115\t    [_ cursor-value]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
