{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md | sed -n '45,85p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1170,1210p'\"","aggregated_output":"    45\tThe session that minted the evaluation is provenance. Record its stable\n    46\tshell token as a fact on a metadata entity and refer to that entity in\n    47\tthe datoms' `m` slot, following the metadata-entity convention; `m` is a\n    48\tlocal integer, not a session string. Preserve the root/round association\n    49\toutside the content-hashed rows. Index code and its claims only: printed\n    50\toutput, last-value history, and ephemeral evaluation results do not enter\n    51\tthe code index by default.\n    52\t\n    53\t## Query surface: owner ruling (2026-09-27)\n    54\t\n    55\t**User require.** `dao.space.query/q` is not bound in the session; the\n    56\tuser's own `(require 'dao.space.query)` binds it, running over the\n    57\tindex this observer maintains. Ruled for `yin.repl`'s explicit, minimal\n    58\tshell contract. Binding `q` at the first prompt (the IDE posture) was\n    59\tconsidered and is a composition a host can still make; the shell does\n    60\tnot. Automatic indexing is a session composition\n    61\tpolicy; exposing an extra language binding is a separate policy. The\n    62\towner can choose the first-prompt posture without changing the medium,\n    63\ttransaction format, or index observer.\n    64\t\n    65\t## Cost and boundary\n    66\t\n    67\tStartup adds one observer attachment and a local index/transactor value;\n    68\tthere is no eager scan of program history or remote fetch. An idle\n    69\tsession performs no indexing work. Each forwarded evaluation pays a\n    70\tlinear pass over its expanded rows, one atomic local transaction for the\n    71\tdatom projection, and the index update; `q` pays its own query cost when\n    72\tcalled. This work is bounded by that program's size and is acceptable as\n    73\tthe cost of making every evaluated program queryable. Publication of\n    74\tcovered indexes can follow the index's normal cadence, outside the\n    75\tevaluation critical path.\n    76\t\n    77\tThis is neither ShiBi authorization nor the `dao.jing.content` service\n    78\tin `dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md`, section 1. It adds no\n    79\twire shape. It composes beside that epic's middleware, remote channel,\n    80\tcontent service, REPL service, UDP, pair, and UCF slices; their transport\n    81\tand content-service file sets need no change for this local observer.\n  1170\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n  1171\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n  1172\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n  1173\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n  1174\t        (let [expanded (try\n  1175\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n  1176\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1177\t                                   :clj Exception\n  1178\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n  1179\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n  1180\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n  1181\t            failed\n  1182\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n  1183\t                  indexed (cond-> expanded\n  1184\t                            (pos? forwarded) run-index-stage)]\n  1185\t              (with-index-notice\n  1186\t                (cond\n  1187\t                  (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\n  1188\t                  [(assoc indexed :ingress-loss? true)\n  1189\t                   (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1190\t\n  1191\t                  (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state indexed)\n  1192\t\n  1193\t                  :else [(assoc indexed :vm (:vm state))\n  1194\t                         (format-expansion-errors errors)])\n  1195\t                (when (pos? forwarded)\n  1196\t                  (index/notice (:indexer expanded)\n  1197\t                                (:indexer indexed)))))))))))\n  1198\t\n  1199\t\n  1200\t(defn- compile-clojure-forms\n  1201\t  [forms]\n  1202\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n  1203\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n  1204\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n  1205\t\n  1206\t\n  1207\t(defn- compile-source\n  1208\t  [lang input]\n  1209\t  (case lang\n  1210\t    :clojure (compile-clojure-forms (read-forms input))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-28 12:59:22 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 19:59:22 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n- **P2 | [index.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-repl-index/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:131) |** The intake is a complete-retention memory log. Every round appends a full-history publication to it ([index.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-repl-index/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:207)), and the log never removes entries ([memory_log.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-repl-index/src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc:1)). Draining advances a cursor but retains all payloads. A long-running REPL therefore keeps roughly quadratic publication data in memory, even after dao.jing has stored it. **Fix:** release each completed publication’s intake while preserving `transactor/publish!`, or obtain an owner ruling for a different publication path.\n\nThe round 1 overflow and failure-visibility findings are fixed: the large-publication test reads every datom back, and a refusing store produces a round warning and index status. The index-gap behavior also follows the owner’s ruling: evaluation continues while indexing remains marked lost until reset.\n\n**Q6.** The retained intake is a shipping defect for a long-running session, beyond the owner-approved cost of publishing every round. Which remedy to adopt is an owner scope decision: option (i) bypasses the specified `transactor/publish!` path; option (ii) changes `dao.space` outside this slice; option (iii) leaves the memory growth in place. The current test proves a large publication succeeds, but does not bound retention across rounds.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES  \nSign-off: WITHHELD"}}
